{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moses, etc.</b> The reason He set apart another utterance in the middle of the matter is to justify what I explained: that the first statement, in which He said <b>they have turned aside</b>, etc., <b>they have made</b>, etc., came only to give the reason for Moses' descent from his rank. But now He comes to speak concerning what pertains to Israel regarding their sin. Therefore He said <b>and He said</b>, etc.; and were it not for this, it would have been understood that the declaration of 'they have turned aside quickly' came only on this account. Understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:35:42.331394557Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}